    "ruleSetVersion": 4,
    "historyDays": 35,
    "fillOrder": [
      "Day by day and unit by unit, in the order night, day, evening, full-time officers whose rotation has them on that day fill the unit's minimum. Only 12 h officers work nights: those who asked for nights first (most senior first), then the newest. Day and evening go first to officers whose preferred time matches, then by seniority. An 8 h officer keeps one block, day or evening, all quarter. Each rank stays on its own posts, here and in every step below: officers fill officer posts and supervisors fill supervisor posts, by seniority inside the rank.",
      "Every other full-time officer whose rotation has them on that day is then rostered too, even above the minimum, so a full-time officer works their full rotation.",
      "Part-time and casual officers (under 1.0 FTE) then fill what is still short, in their home unit only, newest first, up to their FTE \u00d7 80 h in each pay period; a part-time supervisor fills supervisor posts the same way.",
      "Where a unit is closed on a day, its full-time officers may fill another unit's remaining shortage in a post of their own rank (by home unit, then seniority).",
      "Every proposed shift is checked by the rules engine (rule set v4) against the officer's last 35 days of shifts: a Block skips that officer, a warning is kept and counted. Planned leave days are never rostered. Anything still short is a gap, left for a person to fill on the board."
    ]
  }
